---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro'
import UnitGrid from '../components/UnitGrid.astro'
import { committee } from '../data/committee'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="ISO/TC 12 maintains the ISO 80000 series of standards for quantities and units. Founded 1947; secretariat held by SIS (Sweden) since 1982."
>
  <div class="page page--wide">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="About"
      title="Quantities, units, and the work of TC 12"
      lead="Every measurement in science, engineering, and trade rests on a shared vocabulary of <em>quantities</em> (what we measure) and <em>units</em> (how we measure it). ISO/TC 12 maintains that vocabulary."
    />

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="prose-tc">
        <h3>The scope</h3>
        <p>{committee.scope}</p>

        <h3>What TC 12 produces</h3>
        <p>
          The committee's principal work is the <strong>ISO/IEC 80000</strong>
          series — parts covering quantities and units across mathematics,
          space and time, mechanics, thermodynamics, electromagnetism, light,
          acoustics, physical chemistry, atomic and nuclear physics, characteristic
          numbers, condensed matter, and information science.
        </p>
        <p>
          TC 12 also coordinates with <strong>BIPM</strong> (the SI Brochure),
          <strong>JCGM</strong> (the VIM and GUM), <strong>IEC/TC 25</strong>
          (electrical and information-science quantities), and many ISO committees
          that consume its work — from acoustics to health informatics.
        </p>

        <h3>Why it matters</h3>
        <p>
          A watt is a watt everywhere. A kilogram is a kilogram. When a paper
          publishes a measurement, a hospital records a dose, or a satellite
          reports a position, those numbers depend on agreed quantities and
          units. TC 12 is the body that maintains that agreement.
        </p>

        <h3>How to participate</h3>
        <p>
          Participation is through ISO member bodies. National standards bodies
          can join as <strong>P-members</strong> (voting) or <strong>O-members</strong>
          (observers). Individuals are nominated by their member body to serve
          on working groups. Start at
          <a href="https://www.iso.org/members.html">iso.org/members</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="about-aside">
        <div class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Leadership</p>
          <dl class="leadership">
            <div>
              <dt>Chair</dt>
              <dd>{committee.chair}</dd>
              <dd class="muted">until end 2027</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Committee Manager</dt>
              <dd>{committee.committee_manager}</dd>
              <dd class="muted">SIS, Sweden</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Secretariat</dt>
              <dd>{committee.secretariat}</dd>
              <dd class="muted">Since 1982</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">The base units</p>
          <p class="muted" style="margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem;">
            Seven SI base units define the dimensions across which all ISO 80000 quantities live.
          </p>
          <UnitGrid variant="compact" />
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">External</p>
          <ul class="links">
            <li><a href={committee.links.isoCommittee}>ISO committee page ↗</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-brochure">BIPM SI Brochure ↗</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.bipm.org/en/committees/jc/jcgm">JCGM (VIM, GUM) ↗</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr; gap: 3rem; }
  }
  .about-aside { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
  .leadership { margin: 0.75rem 0 0; }
  .leadership div { margin-bottom: 0.875rem; }
  .leadership dt { font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-slate-500); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .leadership dd { margin: 0.125rem 0 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--color-slate-900); font-weight: 500; }
  .dark .leadership dd { color: #fafaf9; }
  .leadership dd.muted { font-weight: 400; color: var(--color-slate-500); font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .links { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0.5rem 0 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .links a { color: var(--color-brand); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .muted { color: var(--color-slate-500); }
</style>
